oes the value  of F of 3 equal well you can see if we  put negative 1 in for X we get negative  1 squared minus 2 times negative 1 plus  1 okay this is 1 plus 2 okay plus 1  which is 4  and if we put three in what do we get  three squared minus two times three plus  one that's nine minus six which is three  plus one equals four so what you can see  is we have negative one four and we have  three comma four and you can see that  they have the same y-value okay so what  that means is that somewhere in between  negative one and three the slope of the  tangent line must be equal to zero and  so what we're going to do now is we're  going to take the derivative so f prime  of x equals 2x minus two we're going to  set that equal to zero okay add two to  both sides and then divide by two and  you can see that that value is going to  be when x equals one one of course is in  between negative 1 and positive 3 and  the slope of the tangent line at that  point is going to be 0 it's going to be  horizontal if you want to graph this  just to understand it a little bit  better this is actually a parabola  that's been shifted right one so it  looks something like this okay and so  over here we have negative 1/4 that's  this point and we have 3/4 that's this  point you can see that they're at the  same height and in between negative 1  and 3 there's a point in this case it's  at positive 1 where the horizontal you  know the tangent line is horizontal at  zero now it happens to be right you know  in between right in the middle at the  midpoint that's not always the case I  just did this as a simple example just  so I can show you the graph and just  kind of show you how it works but again  you want to make sure that it satisfies  all these conditions continuous  differentiable and that the the Y values  at both of the endpoints are the same  and then that apply rolls theorem  applies meaning the in between those two  endpoints the tangent line has to be  horizontal so let's look at a